	"title"	"Viewpoint Threat Detector"
	"description"	"[h1]Viewpoint Threat Detector[/h1]
Improve situational awareness in Project Zomboid, especially when playing with Project Viewpoint's limited field of view.
Detect nearby A-Life NPCs, approaching zombies, and dangerous sprinters through customizable visual alerts, directional indicators, and warning sounds.

[h2]A-Life NPC Detection[/h2]
[h3]Stance and Threat Detection[/h3]
[list]
[*]Choose which NPC stances trigger alerts: Hostile, Careful, Neutral, Friendly, and Allied.
[*]When multiple stances are detected, alerts prioritize Hostile, Careful, Neutral, Friendly, then Allied.
[*]Each stance has its own alert color for easier identification.
[*]Alerts can display distance, directional indicators, and NPC faction information.
[*]Optionally identify nearby A-Life NPCs carrying firearms.
[*]Unknown factions follow A-Life's default Hostile stance.
[*]With Project A-Life Jimmy, the player's own people and allied standing are recognized as Allied.
[/list]
[h3]Close Hostile Warnings[/h3]
[list]
[*]Optional proximity alarm when a Hostile A-Life NPC gets close.
[*]Configure its detection distance, warning sound, and volume independently.
[/list]

[h2]Zombie Detection[/h2]
[h3]Rear Zombie Alerts[/h3]
[list]
[*]Detect regular zombies approaching from behind, with directional indicators pointing toward the nearest threat.
[*]Balanced rear detection is enabled by default: 3.5 tiles normally and 6.5 tiles with the Keen Hearing trait.
[*]Alternatively, configure a custom detection range and angle.
[*]Optional same-floor, line-of-sight, and fallen-zombie filters.
[*]Customizable warning sound and volume.
[/list]
[h3]Sprinter Alerts[/h3]
[list]
[*]Dedicated warnings for nearby sprinters, separate from regular zombie detection.
[*]Independent detection distance and alarm range.
[*]Configure same-floor and line-of-sight checks.
[*]Optionally ignore fallen sprinters.
[*]Independent warning sound and volume.
[/list]

[h2]Customizable Warning Sounds[/h2]
[list]
[*]Configure independent sounds and volume levels for regular rear-zombie alerts, close Hostile A-Life NPCs, and sprinters.
[*]Choose from built-in sounds, including heartbeat, radar and sonar pings, soft beeps, short alarms, and additional audio cues.
[*]Default sounds: heartbeat for regular zombies, radar ping for close Hostile NPCs, and sonar ping for sprinters.
[*]Preview selected sounds in-game using a configurable preview key, with the same playback behavior as real alerts. The key is unassigned by default to avoid conflicts with gameplay controls.
[*]Regular alarm sounds apply to zombie alerts by default; Hostile NPC and sprinter alarms are controlled separately.
[/list]

[h2]HUD and Visual Customization[/h2]
[h3]Display Modes[/h3]
[list]
[*]Choose Compact NeatUI, Full NeatUI, or Vanilla Mode for A-Life alert cards. Full NeatUI is selected by default; zombie and sprinter tracking always uses DayZ-style radial indicators.
[*]Full cards can show NPC factions, threat information, distance, and direction.
[*]Minimal mode emphasizes icons, threat counts, distance, and directional indicators.
[*]Immersive mode hides all visual alerts while keeping detection and configured warning sounds active.
[*]A-Life alert cards can be repositioned by dragging them; radial indicators remain centered on the screen.
[*]Preview sample NPC, rear-zombie, and sprinter alerts directly from Mod Options.
[/list]
[h3]Directional Indicators[/h3]
[list]
[*]When Viewpoint Compass is active, directional arrows follow the camera heading; otherwise, they follow the character's facing direction.
[*]Customize the radial circle radius, icon size, distance fade, close/far colors, blink distance, and number of directions shown.
[*]Sprinters have a separate all-direction radial alert, independent of regular zombie indicators.
[/list]
[h3]Interface Compatibility[/h3]
[list]
[*]The two NeatUI styles use NeatUI_Framework panel backgrounds when it is installed.
[*]Falls back to the standard HUD when NeatUI is unavailable.
[/list]

[h2]Vehicle Alert Behavior[/h2]
[list]
[*]Configure alert suppression independently for rear zombies, sprinters, and A-Life NPCs.
[*]All three alert categories are disabled inside vehicles by default.
[*]Existing saves automatically migrate the previous vehicle alert setting.
[/list]

[h2]Requirements and Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Project Zomboid Build 42.20+.
[*]Project A-Life is required for NPC stance, faction, firearm, and close-hostile detection.
[*]Rear-zombie and sprinter detection work independently without Project A-Life.
[*]Viewpoint Compass is optional and enables camera-relative directional indicators and the A-Life marker integration.
[*]NeatUI_Framework is optional and provides alternative HUD styling.
[/list]

[h2]Latest features[/h2]
[list]
[*]Optional The Mutants support adds all-direction indicators that blend from dark green to neon green as they approach. Its category independently configures visual and alarm distances, blink distance, direction limit, floor/path/fallen filters, vehicle suppression, colors and previews. Mutants use a separate local alarm with its own toggle, sound (Space - Wall by default) and volume. Mutants have separate sectors and do not trigger ordinary zombie or purple sprinter indicators. Requires The Mutants public identity API.
[*]Zombie tracking uses DayZ-style radial indicators only. Circular arcs sit around a screen-centered radius and point toward detected threats.
[*]Regular rear-zombie indicators blink within a configurable critical distance (1.5 tiles by default); low climbable fences do not block the default line-of-sight check.
[*]Sprinter indicators cover all directions, transition from magenta to purple with distance, and blink within a configurable distance (4 tiles by default).
[*]Set rear-zombie and sprinter indicator limits independently from 1 to 8 directions (2 each by default); each direction represents its nearest threat.
[*]A-Life stance alerts are disabled by default while this alert system is being redesigned. When Viewpoint Compass is installed locally, nearby A-Life NPC positions and stance colors can also appear on its compass; enable the marker option in Compass to activate this bridge.
[*]Stay With Me companions are excluded from zombie and sprinter detection, including counts, indicators, and warning alarms.
[*]The optional alert preview can show every A-Life stance and both radial indicator types without nearby threats.
[*]Rear-zombie detection follows the camera heading when Viewpoint Compass is active, instead of the character's facing direction.
[/list]

Workshop ID: 3812396995
Mod ID: 3812396995/ALifeThreatAlert"
	"changenote"	"1.4.82: Add The Mutants detection with fully independent ranges, filters, blinking, indicator limits, vehicle controls, colors and local alarm settings. Default mutant sound: Space - Wall."
}
